  <title>
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">Enhancing Food Security, Nutrition and Resilience of the Most Food Insecure and Vulnerable Host Communities and Asylum Seekers in Upper East and Upper West Regions of Ghana</narrative>
  </title>
  <description>
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">In line with the Gulf of Guinea Joint Response Plan for Ghana, this project aims to contribute to addressing food insecurity and malnutrition as well as build resilience of vulnerable asylum seekers and host communities in Upper East and Upper West regions of Ghana. The International Organization for Migration is achieving this through an approach which integrates asset creation and livelihood strengthening, school feeding, prevention and treatment of malnutrition, and social and behaviour change communications. The project adopts an evidence-based approach, stemming from the roll out of the Solutions and Mobility Index, which identifies fragility levels related to food security and nutrition. This informs the implementation of training by the Organization on sustainable agricultural practices and eco-friendly business ventures.</narrative>
  </description>
